  "raw": " heaven sent! Armed with deep carbon nanotube anti-armor plating in systems containing bone plates as heavy as 500kilos the US troops were able to fight Soviet Russian Infrastructure across in around twenty minutes.\"\n– Robert Zemeckis (will love you forever) (if he doesn't mind me republishing this all over again)\n\nI'm already working on an action series fighting fictional filipinos against a reality TV lead assassin from hell after I get my DBA for copyright claim. Still need another rooms idea though...\n\nWhy not have the player look through a lens with color coded lenses corresponding to enemy locations scattered around the battlefield? The user can then decide which is what before running up to it to eliminate them like a star wars style game but with more accurate somewhat 3D potential guns, etc. Most importantly being able to shoot the lenses would hurt or kill the crowd regardless if they're known enemies but for each newly respawned one it trigger a camera recording",
  "serialized": "heaven sent! Armed with deep carbon nanotube anti-armor plating in systems containing bone plates as heavy as 500kilos the US troops were able to fight Soviet Russian Infrastructure across in around twenty minutes.\" – Robert Zemeckis (will love you forever) (if he doesn't mind me republishing this all over again) I'm already working on an action series fighting fictional filipinos against a reality TV lead assassin from hell after I get my DBA for copyright claim. Still need another rooms idea though... Why not have the player look through a lens with color coded lenses corresponding to enemy locations scattered around the battlefield? The user can then decide which is what before running up to it to eliminate them like a star wars style game but with more accurate somewhat 3D potential guns, etc. Most importantly being able to shoot the lenses would hurt or kill the crowd regardless if they're known enemies but for each newly respawned one it trigger a camera recording",
